  "scenario": "With stock Plasma running, compare an IPv4 control, the combined profile, and the restored control at fixed EQOS interrupt affinity CPU6. Each phase uses four eight-second iperf3 transfers and 128 paced 512-byte UDP echo pairs. The combined profile sets receive watchdog count 64, transmit IOC interval 8, and ordinary IPv4 header and TCP checksum flags plus UDP receive checksum. Run separate single-echo transmit retirement and peer checksum checks. Restore the initial graphics DTB Ethernet policy.",
  "expected": "The combined profile preserves delivery and reduces process CPU for TCP in both directions. The peer sees valid checksums on ordinary UDP and preserves an explicitly omitted IPv4 UDP checksum.",
  "observed": "TCP receiver throughput stayed above 933 Mbit/s with zero retransmissions. Board iperf3 CPU fell for TCP receive and rose for TCP transmit. Combined UDP receive lost 180 of 205998 datagrams, all in one interval near 5–6 seconds. The target UDP full-socket-buffer counter rose by 180. Bad checksum, bad length, and no-socket deltas were zero. All 128 echo pairs arrived in each phase. The single transmit tail reached local q0 idle. The peer saw the expected 0xffff, 0xfffe, and explicit 0x0000 UDP checksums.",
  "duration_seconds": null,
